    // was already passing only by an accidental substring coincidence ("11 record(s)..." contains "1 record(s)
    // ..."), against task/gate records an UNAUTHORISED test machine legitimately creates of its own accord as an
    // ordinary "work generation" side effect of raising any gate -- all correctly LOW-severity/disclosed, never
    // failing D033 (`ok` passes; only the test's own over-strict count assertion did not). Writing the floor adds
    // exactly two more such legitimate discovery records (P2-AR-0081.checkpoint.md has the instrumented counts),
    // pushing 11 to 13 and breaking the lucky coincidence -- not a security regression. `tests/certification/
